 2. 🧑‍⚖️ Scoop: ACLU eyes court flips 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Allie Carl/Axios The American Civil Liberties Union is expanding its state Supreme Court election fight into deep-red territory after the midterms left Texas just one judicial seat away from a Democratic majority, the group tells Axios' Russell Contreras exclusively. 

 The next battles over abortion, voting rights, redistricting, religion in schools and LGBTQ protections could hinge on state Supreme Court races that are often overshadowed by federal campaigns. 👀 By the numbers: The ACLU's chief political and advocacy officer Deirdre Schifeling tells Axios that it's eyeing Supreme Court races in 11 states in 2027 and 2028.

 The group worked on court elections in five states this year. It spent $30 million on its broader electoral program, with Supreme Court races claiming the biggest share. Go deeper . 

 
 
