 4. 📸 Pic to go: Lights-out football 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo: Julia Demaree Nikhinson/AP The lights at Maryland's Northwest Stadium went out during the third quarter of last night's NFL game between the Cincinnati Bengals and the Washington Commanders, leading to a four-minute delay.

 The Commanders were in the red zone, trailing 10-7, when the stadium went dark. 💡 ESPN said a stadium vendor didn't disable the regular maintenance scheduled for 10 p.m. ET on weekdays.

 After a brief timeout, the lights came back on and the game resumed. The Commanders eventually won 22-20 on a walk-off field goal. Go deeper . 

 
 
